#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
analyze_runs.py — Watchdog run analyzer

Which tool? Run `python3 scripts/analyze_runs.py which-tool` for the full routing table.
  - Run artifacts               → this tool (analyze_runs.py)
  - Dedicated FL front door     → python3 scripts/analyze_failure_log.py <cmd>
  - Watchdog JS source          → python3 scripts/watchdog_source.py <cmd>
  - Game / server C++           → Grep tool; see docs/agent/agents.md § WG patterns
  - Git history (watchdog)      → python3 scripts/watchdog_source.py diff|log

Subcommands:
  list       Tabular summary of all runs (newest first)
  diff       Gate-by-gate comparison of two runs
  trend      Gate state history across runs
  search     Filter runs by verdict, commit, branch, gate, date
  show       Full details for a single run
  gates      All known gate names with failure/null counts
  pickup-chain Post-run same-item pickup proof from recorder/recording.jsonl
  death-window Summarize death→respawn windows, including inventory/item overlap
  triage     Compact post-run summary for agent triage (<=25 lines)
  fl         Query docs/FAILURE_LOG.md: add, search, audit, lane-audit, multiplayer-preflight, card, gates, list, validate, fix-attempt, prior-attempts, correlate, error-scan, epochs, epoch-statuses
  fl context  Native FL/card/required-fields context
  contract   Print the watchdog artifact/recorder architecture contract
  which-tool Print query-space routing table

Post-run punch-card recipe workflow:
  python3 scripts/watchdog_recipe_store.py capture-from-run <run-id> --recipe-name <name>
  python3 scripts/watchdog_run_canonical.py --controller-mode recipe --controller-recipe <name> ...
"""

